// expect: 42
// SYNTAX §«Partial application — the product with a hole»: a parameter
// product constructed with a field left unsupplied IS a value, and the
// spec's own headline example writes no `??` at all —
// `let adults = filter(.age > 18)`, reused twice. The bare positional
// prefix is that spelling.
//
// It did not compile. `add(1)` typed clean and emitted `(call $add)` with
// two operands where three were expected, so wat2wasm — an oracle outside
// the medium — was what caught it. The `??`-marked twin
// (`add(??, 41)`) ran correctly the whole time, which is what made the
// gap legible: the mint was built and only the decider refused.
fn add(a, b) = a + b

fn main() = {
  let inc = add(1)
  inc(41)
}
